      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f318f198b38ac71ff34f726|full_name}: FBX is reasonably consistent. Either you have the all text format, or you have the all binary format.\n\nVRM mixes text and binary in a way which is awkward for the implementor. Having a blob of metadata alongside binary blobs is fine, the issue is that the method of parsing text and binary is so different that you end up writing multiple parsers to read the format. It’s convenient for one use case where you are a browser and JSON parsing is available in the library.\n\nMinecraft has demonstrated how to do metadata in binary, see  https://wiki.vg/NBT",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
